# Attribute policy.
#
# Line endings: `* text=auto eol=lf` below makes the repository canonical form LF
# regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf. That matters more here than in a
# typical project: tools/gui-check.mjs compares generated artifacts BYTE-FOR-BYTE
# against a fresh assembly of their sources, so committed bytes must not depend
# on local git configuration.
#
# The 136-CRLF / 78-LF split this repository used to have was normalised to LF in
# the same commit that added this file. `runtime/bridge/src/parts/**` are
# function-body fragments that Prettier cannot parse and are excluded from
# formatting, but their line endings are normalised like everything else — the
# bundler joins them with "\n" and gui-check compares the result, so LF-only is
# the state that keeps both sides identical.
#
# Windows launchers keep CRLF: cmd.exe and some PowerShell hosts are unhappy with
# LF-only script files.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never attempt a text diff or an EOL conversion.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pak binary
*.bin binary
*.dat binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# Vendored native dependency: real source, but not ours to reformat.
runtime/inject/third_party/** -diff
